Hint:\(\lambda = \dfrac{h}{p}\)

Let the momentum of e-at any time t is p and its de-Broglie wavelength is λ.
Then,\(p = { h \over \lambda}\)
\(\begin{aligned} &
\frac{\mathrm{dp}}{\mathrm{dt}}=\frac{-\mathrm{h}}{\lambda^2} \frac{\mathrm{~d}
\lambda}{\mathrm{dt}} \\ & \mathrm{ma}=\mathrm{F}=-\frac{\mathrm{h}}{\lambda}
\frac{\mathrm{~d} \lambda}{\mathrm{dt}}\left[\mathrm{~m}=\text { mass of }
\mathrm{e}^{-}\right] \end{aligned}\)
Where, -ve sign represents decrease in\(\lambda\)with time
\(\mathrm{ma}=\frac{-\mathrm{h}}{(\mathrm{~h} / \mathrm{p})^2} \frac{\mathrm{~d}
\lambda}{\mathrm{dt}}\)
\(\begin{aligned} & \mathrm{a}=-\frac{\mathrm{p}^2}{\mathrm{mh}}
\frac{\mathrm{~d} \lambda}{\mathrm{dt}} \\ & a=-\frac{m v^2}{h} \frac{d
\lambda}{d t} \\ & \frac{\mathrm{~d}
\lambda}{\mathrm{dt}}=-\frac{\mathrm{ah}}{\mathrm{mv}^2} \ldots \ldots(1) \\ &
\text { here, } \mathrm{a}=\frac{\mathrm{qE}}{\mathrm{~m}}=\frac{e}{\mathrm{~m}}
\frac{\sigma}{2 s_0} \\ & \mathrm{a}=\frac{\sigma \mathrm{e}}{2 \mathrm{~m}
\varepsilon_0} \text { and } \mathrm{v}=\mathrm{u}+\mathrm{at} \\ &
\mathrm{v}=\mathrm{at} \end{aligned}\)
Substituting values of a and in equation(1)
\(\begin{aligned} & \frac{\mathrm{d} \lambda}{\mathrm{dt}}=-\frac{2 \mathrm{~h}
\varepsilon_0}{\sigma e \mathrm{t}^2} \\ & \Rightarrow \frac{d \lambda}{d t}
\propto \frac{1}{t^2} \\ & \Rightarrow \mathrm{n}=2 \end{aligned}\)<div style="margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;"><div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style="padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color:#d97706;">🟡 Medium · 68% Got This Correct</span></div><div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;"><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(1)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">18%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;"><div style="color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;">(2) ✓</div><div style="font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;">68%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(3)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">12%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(4)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">3%</div></div></div></div>

Hint:\(\lambda=\frac{h}{p}\)

Step 1: Find the relation for de-Broglie wavelength in terms of electric
potential.
The de-Broglie wavelength of an electron is given by;
\(\lambda=\frac{h}{p}=\frac{h}{\sqrt{2m_eK}}\)
Kinetic energy of an electron accelerated by a voltage is given by;
\(K=eV\)
Therefore, the de-Broglie wavelength in terms of electric potential would be;
\(\lambda=\frac{h}{\sqrt{2m_eeV}}~~~...(1)\)
Step 2: Find the de-Broglie wavelength of an electron.
Substitute the known values in equation (1);
\(\lambda=\frac{6.6\times10^{-34}}{\sqrt{2\times 9.1\times 10^{-31}\times
1.6\times 10^{-19} \times 50}}=1.7\times10^{-10}\ m\)
Therefore;
\(\Rightarrow \lambda=1.7~\mathring{A} \)
Hence, option(4)is the correct answer.<div style="margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;"><div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style="padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.15); color:#16a34a;">🟢 Easy · 72% Got This Correct</span></div><div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;"><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(1)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">8%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(2)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">12%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(3)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">9%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;"><div style="color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;">(4) ✓</div><div style="font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;">73%</div></div></div></div>

